#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/mr.rc -- Marathi (मराठी), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "mr"`.
//
// Stage E108, group A: the translation is an adaptation (decision 198.14), not a literal one.
// The terms of Windows are those of Windows in Marathi; the polite imperative of Marathi
// (-आ: करा, निवडा) addresses the reader without gender; the author speaks in the masculine
// (RULES 14). Where each string is seen and how much room it has is res/lang/context.tsv.
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Marathi — `[general] language = "mr"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
